WEBVTT

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.730
Kotshuna Mountains, Sho

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:12.900
So listen, the coalition army that Ri Boku's leading?

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.110
They're already attacking Kankoku Pass!

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:18.190
Hoo-whee! Chin's goose is as good as cooked!

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:20.650
Serves 'em right.

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.280
No, Ryo Kusui--we can't.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:35.110
I realize that Chin is in for one terrible fight.

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:39.690
But I made up my mind
when I left the Hi Shin Force:

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:42.980
I wouldn't come back until
I had avenged my sister Shou.

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:49.860
So that's why, this time,

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.690
I'm going to trust them.

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:25.070
Charge!

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:28.650
After him, troops!

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.650
"Hi"

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:32.860
Charge, Hi Shin Force!

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:37.480
We're gonna be the ones
who get this war started!

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:44.190
The kingdom of Chin had mobilized
all its troops against the coalition army.

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:50.980
Their battle got underway at last
on the battlefield at Kankoku Pass.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:55.400
Smash these Chin brats to pieces!

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:59.360
Just try it, you Sho nobodies!

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:03.940
Plow on through, Hi Shin Force!

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:04.940
Right!

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:08.070
Get 'em good!

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:14.040
Two Battlefields

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:14.690
That's the way!

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:17.230
The Hi Shin Force is fighting remarkably well.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:21.360
But even more than that...

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:24.780
...Lord Hyou's inner-right army
is an absolute terror.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:28.780
It's like there are hundreds
of Lord Hyous out there.

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:29.780
Mmm-hmm.

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:34.650
But one thing that doesn't make sense
is the Sho army's response.

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:38.190
Ri Haku Army HQ

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:38.190
"Sho"

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:38.730
That's Ri Haku.

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:42.940
He's one of those generals
who uses all kinds of tricks.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:48.110
But right now he's doing nothing strategic--
just fighting.

00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:49.900
Why is that?

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:53.780
Ri Haku, sir, why haven't we used
a diagonal formation?

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:56.400
It's not too late to take a defensive stance.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.070
Those are our orders.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:01.730
Orders? From Ri Boku?

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:03.690
No.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:06.930
Coalition Army HQ

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:07.440
We don't need to visit Sho's headquarters?

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:14.360
Our numbers may be greater, but honestly,
Lord Hyou is a dangerous foe.

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:16.280
Shun Shin Kun.

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:22.360
Just as you have unwavering confidence
in General Kan Mei of the So army,

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:25.480
I've put my fullest trust in one man as well.

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:28.490
Sho Army HQ

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:29.070
The Sho army's tactician:

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:32.460
Sho Army Adjutant

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:31.780
my adjutant, Kei Sha.

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:32.940
Sir!

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:37.110
Ri Haku's army seems to be
struggling more than expected!

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.860
Let them be.

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:43.440
I doubt even Lord Hyou expects
to get past that dense Ri Haku Army

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:46.820
with just a simple charge.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:50.530
Though it may look like
they're striking at random,

00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:54.650
in truth, he's come in search
of a place to light a fire.

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:55.650
A fire?

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:56.860
No...

00:04:56.860 --> 00:05:01.690
Perhaps it's more correct to say
he's come to <i>make</i> that place.

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:04.650
When you're up against someone like that,

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:11.190
it's wise not to allow them to find purchase
for their talons in the early stages.

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:12.730
If you can do that,

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:16.230
their utter bewilderment will begin to show.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:19.570
Huh?

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:22.780
We've caught up to Lord Hyou's unit!

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:25.650
They're looking fatigued, all right...

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:28.280
Something's off!

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:30.280
This battlefield--

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:33.110
it smells of nothing!

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:36.530
You're saying Kei Sha can predict
Lord Hyou's moves?

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:37.780
Yes.

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:41.530
Kei Sha must be one remarkable man.

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:48.820
But it's nearly impossible to predict
what Lord Hyou will do, wild beast that he is.

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:55.570
I may be a clever general, yet there are some
moves of his even I cannot predict.

00:05:55.570 --> 00:06:00.610
But Kei Sha understands Lord Hyou.

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:02.110
Understands him?

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:03.440
Yes.

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:08.570
You see, Kei Sha and Lord Hyou
are birds of a feather:

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:11.280
both generals act on instinct.

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:14.400
Kai Dou!

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:16.980
Send the front row to the back
and let them recover!

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:18.320
Sir!

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:19.400
Kai Bou!

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:22.030
Bring the middle and back rows forward!

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:22.780
Sir!

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:25.070
We're moving into our second charge!

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:27.030
Roger!

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:31.570
Kei Sha, sir! There's a large dust cloud
where Lord Hyou's army is positioned!

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:38.440
He's rearranging his troops
in preparation for their next charge.

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:42.440
The time is right. Very well.

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:45.730
Send Kou Son Ryuu's right-flank army
forward ten paces!

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:51.110
Eh? Y-Yes, sir!

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:55.030
A slight fluctuation in
the detached unit to the left.

00:06:55.030 --> 00:06:57.940
I smell a rat.

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:02.480
Now <i>this</i> is interesting!

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:04.860
Onward to the left!

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:09.860
A huge dust cloud in their midst!

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:12.900
The right! Lord Hyou's army
is heading to the right!

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:16.360
Is this because Kou Son Ryuu's army shifted?

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:17.650
Got him.

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:20.320
Forward!

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:21.360
Move it!

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:24.650
Clear a path! Orders from headquarters!

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:27.530
Now Sho's left flank is on the move!

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:31.690
Are they forcing their way
<i>through</i> their ally Ri Haku's army?

00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:35.360
The left-flank army broke into a run
at Kei Sha's command.

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:42.810
Left Wing

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:35.220
