00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:40.180
{=2}Lord Hyou army

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:40.230
{=2}Lord Hyou army

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:40.310
{=2}Lord Hyou army

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:41.140
{=2}Lord Hyou army

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:41.190
{=2}Lord Hyou army

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:42.390
{=2}Lord Hyou army

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:42.940
This meant

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:42.480
{=2}Lord Hyou army

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:42.810
{=2}Lord Hyou army

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:49.360
Man Goku's left-flank army was attacking
the very last row of Lord Hyou's army,

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:49.570
Sho Army General

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:51.320
full of exhausted troops.

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:55.070
Lord Hyou!

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:58.570
Th-The enemy is attacking our rearmost ranks!

00:07:58.570 --> 00:08:03.900
Targeting a weakened area
is an ironclad rule of nature.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:05.980
How do you like that, Lord Hyou?

00:08:05.980 --> 00:08:09.320
The fire has been lit here on our battlefield--

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:12.860
under <i>you</i> , that is.

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:16.070
H-How's our rear guard?

00:08:16.070 --> 00:08:17.900
I can't tell from here!

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:20.230
We must go assist them at once!

00:08:20.230 --> 00:08:24.150
Our exhausted troops were rotated out
to those rearmost ranks!

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:26.440
I-It's no use!

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:27.780
What?!

00:08:27.780 --> 00:08:31.690
The flow of troops is moving
entirely in this direction.

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:34.530
Going against that flow
and reaching the very back?

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:36.400
It can't be done!

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:40.730
Even if it <i>were</i> possible,
our formation would be in total disarray.

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:45.070
If we move forward, then, and circle around
toward the rear from the outside...

00:08:45.070 --> 00:08:48.030
You think they'd hold out that long?!

00:08:48.030 --> 00:08:51.610
We... we're out of options.

00:08:56.480 --> 00:08:58.530
Shin! Behind us!

00:08:58.530 --> 00:09:00.650
Lord Hyou's stopped, too!

00:09:02.820 --> 00:09:06.230
So Sho's general Kei Sha
is the instinctive type?

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:07.650
He is.

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:13.070
I've seen him a few times...
and he didn't seem that way to me.

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:19.110
Not all instinctive generals are like Lord Hyou.

00:09:19.110 --> 00:09:25.820
For every man like Lord Hyou,
a lion who finds his prey and attacks it violently...

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:32.440
...there's a spider who sets a trap
to ensnare his prey

00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:36.650
and waits for it to enter of its own free will.

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:40.940
And when someone's caught in that web,

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:45.480
soon they'll find themselves unable to move.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:47.530
"The Silent Hunter."

00:09:47.530 --> 00:09:51.610
Of all the instinctive generals,
the one I find the most formidable

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:52.860
is Kei Sha.

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:58.480
A one-sided battle against Lord Hyou's army...

00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:01.070
Watch how Man Goku's army attacks!

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:03.780
The enemy's rear ranks are in tatters!

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:06.110
Ri Haku, sir, this must be...

00:10:06.110 --> 00:10:11.110
Mmm. A truly unforgiving trap, that formation.

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:16.440
Unable to move, Lord Hyou's army
will go on to lose its rear ranks.

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:23.530
Here I'd heard Lord Hyou's shrewd intuition
kept him <i>out</i> of enemy traps.

00:10:23.530 --> 00:10:26.230
According to Kei Sha,

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:30.820
this Lord Hyou fellow is highly attuned
to the battlefield and battle status,

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:33.820
based on the opposing army's position,
its relative size--

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:38.030
even their troops' emotions
and where they're looking.

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:44.150
But to put it another way, without all that,
he picks up on <i>nothing</i> .

00:10:44.150 --> 00:10:49.320
Which is why Kei Sha didn't breathe
of a word of this strategy to me.

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:50.480
Huh?

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:56.190
What's more, he forbade me
from using any tricks with my army here.

00:10:56.190 --> 00:11:00.530
That's how he lured Lord Hyou into his trap.

00:11:00.530 --> 00:11:05.360
Lord Hyou's defeat came of not
knowing General Kei Sha.

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:11.230
Magnificent indeed, Kei Sha, sir!

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:17.110
Why not have Kou Son Ryuu's right-flank
army clash with Lord Hyou's army head-on

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:19.980
so we can finish this in one fell swoop?

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:26.070
Sir?

00:11:26.070 --> 00:11:28.150
Quiet.

00:11:28.150 --> 00:11:29.570
Do you hear that?

00:11:29.570 --> 00:11:31.860
Concentrate on your eyes and ears.

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:37.940
The sound of Man Goku's ruthless fangs bearing
down on Lord Hyou's immobilized army,

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:40.980
tearing their very flesh.

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:48.150
This is the best part.

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:53.780
K-Kill them! R-Remember our g-grudge!

00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:57.320
T-Take it out--
take it <i>all</i> out on them!

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:58.360
This is awful!

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:03.820
The rear ranks of Lord Hyou's army
don't have the strength to fend off the foe!

00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:08.190
At this rate, they'll lose
nearly half their number!

00:12:08.190 --> 00:12:10.480
H-Half?!

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:16.190
This started out as 120,000 versus 40,000--
if they lose half of that...

00:12:16.190 --> 00:12:20.440
Wh-What is Lord Hyou's army even doing?

00:12:20.440 --> 00:12:23.110
There's nothing they <i>can</i> do.

00:12:23.110 --> 00:12:26.610
Their only hope is for Lord Hyou
to circle around to the back

00:12:26.610 --> 00:12:29.530
and boost their morale.

00:12:29.530 --> 00:12:32.980
But until that happens...

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:35.280
O-Onward!

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:38.230
Dammit!

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:39.900
Die!

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:43.900
Wha--

00:12:49.150 --> 00:12:51.820
Den Yuu! Den Ei! Hoist the flags!

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:53.900
"Hi"

00:12:53.900 --> 00:12:54.780
"Chin"

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:02.780
The counterattack begins now!

00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:05.070
Say your prayers, Sho scrubs!

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:13.110
Shin!

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:16.360
Our captain and the others-- <i>behind</i> them?!

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:20.030
That's them, all right.
I can see the Hi Shin Force flags clear as day!

00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:24.440
They should have gotten there
well before the rest. How on earth--

00:13:24.440 --> 00:13:28.980
How? There's only one way
they could have done that!

00:13:28.980 --> 00:13:33.440
Y-You don't mean...
They ran against that current?!

00:13:46.110 --> 00:13:49.780
Man, our captain sure makes us
do some crazy stuff.

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:58.070
What's wrong, Lord Hyou's men? That all you got?

00:13:58.070 --> 00:14:00.650
Don't be openin' your back up to the enemy

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:03.400
just 'cause you got a little outta breath!

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:05.780
Are you kidding me?

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:07.900
We were the vanguard! We got absolutely--

00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:10.440
Like I give a damn!

00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:15.570
The war's just gettin' started,
but <i>these</i> guys are here to finish it already!

00:14:15.570 --> 00:14:18.530
This here is our moment of truth!

00:14:18.530 --> 00:14:22.940
Lord Hyou's men: If you gotta lean on somebody,
grab onto Shin of the Hi Shin Force

00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:25.730
and get yourselves back in the game!

00:14:25.730 --> 00:14:26.610
Wha--

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:28.570
You making fun of us, brat?

00:14:28.570 --> 00:14:30.780
Who do you think you're talking to?

00:14:30.780 --> 00:14:32.650
Ten Bu Force! About face!

00:14:33.980 --> 00:14:38.730
You, too, Nan Shou Force! Fall in behind!

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:41.110
Yuu To Force! Assume charge position!

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:42.980
Call up the troops out back, too!

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:46.150
Lord Hyou's men are responding!

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:48.570
They want to fight alongside us!

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:53.110
Was... was Shin always planning
to lead the troops in the rear?

00:14:53.110 --> 00:14:56.900
N-Nah... like... <i>lead</i> them?

00:14:56.900 --> 00:15:00.980
I mean... the rear guard
has some 10,000 troops!

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:04.730
Let's go, gang! Victory is behind us!

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:06.820
Charge!

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:11.110
Lord Hyou! Behind us!

00:15:11.110 --> 00:15:14.440
The rear guard's turned around
and is on the attack!

00:15:14.440 --> 00:15:16.400
Where'd <i>that</i> come from?

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:18.610
I heard some kind of speech...

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:20.610
Who was it?

00:15:20.610 --> 00:15:22.940
Can't you two tell?

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:29.110
That boy just stirred up one hell of a fire.

00:15:29.110 --> 00:15:33.650
But for him to show up there...

00:15:33.650 --> 00:15:36.820
He must have moved with some speed.

00:15:36.820 --> 00:15:38.610
Did he act on instinct?

00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:43.230
So you're one of us, too.

00:15:43.230 --> 00:15:47.900
You might not have noticed it yourself, boy,

00:15:47.900 --> 00:15:53.150
but the talents of an instinctive warrior
are awakening within you.

00:15:53.150 --> 00:15:57.150
Ha! The man who inherits Ou Ki's poleax

00:15:57.150 --> 00:16:00.110
turns out to be the instinctive type.

00:16:00.110 --> 00:16:03.610
Kai Dou, get back in formation!

00:16:03.610 --> 00:16:05.400
We're heading back there, too?

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:07.690
Don't be ridiculous.

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:11.360
The battlefield is undergoing a major upheaval.

00:16:11.360 --> 00:16:17.860
<i>Now</i> my prey is the Sho general
cowering in the back!

00:16:17.860 --> 00:16:21.230
Kei Sha, sir! Man Goku's army
is under enemy attack!

00:16:21.230 --> 00:16:24.780
Absurd! Their rear ranks, still going strong?

00:16:28.320 --> 00:16:30.780
It's been a long, long time

00:16:30.780 --> 00:16:33.400
since I last fought someone like me.

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:34.650
We're off!

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:44.480
Kankoku Pass

00:16:39.820 --> 00:16:41.570
Meanwhile...

00:16:44.780 --> 00:16:47.280
That wall's impossibly high...

00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:49.230
A ladder only reaches halfway!

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:54.200
Chin General

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:54.360
Those ladders are getting you nowhere!

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:59.110
The Gi soldiers must be hungry
after their long journey.

00:16:59.110 --> 00:17:02.820
Don't underestimate Kankoku Pass--
our kingdom's gateway.

00:17:02.820 --> 00:17:04.900
Now eat your fill...

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:06.960
Chin General

00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:07.190
...of our finest arrows.

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:19.400
Commanding General of Gi

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:23.390
Kan Ki Army 
Battalion Commander

00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:24.030
B-B-Bossman! Ch-Check this out!

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:29.360
Pling!

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:38.280
I got one! I hit someone--did you see that?

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:42.820
O Gi Ko may be mocked as the worst archer
in Kan Ki's army, but my arrow--

00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:44.860
it hit the mark at last!

00:17:44.860 --> 00:17:47.360
Praise me, bossman!

00:17:47.360 --> 00:17:50.110
Well done, O Gi Ko.

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:51.820
Right? Right?

00:17:53.190 --> 00:17:55.610
Of <i>course</i> he'd hit someone.

00:17:55.610 --> 00:17:59.030
There's something I've been meaning
to ask you, boss:

00:17:59.030 --> 00:18:01.320
Why'd you put <i>him</i> in charge of a thousand men?

00:18:03.570 --> 00:18:04.980
Because it's funny.

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:08.280
Okay, everybody--follow O Gi Ko!

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:23.820
Onward!

00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:42.940
Something's coming! Something <i>weird</i> !

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:53.520
Chou Tou Army HQ

00:18:50.860 --> 00:18:52.110
It's a siege tower!

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:53.940
A siege tower, headed this way!

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:56.280
Mou Gou Army HQ

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:56.900
Mou Gou, sir...

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:59.230
So they <i>did</i> bring it with them.

00:19:08.820 --> 00:19:10.690
Boss, what <i>is</i> that?

00:19:11.860 --> 00:19:14.900
Finally something interesting
comes on the scene.

00:19:14.900 --> 00:19:17.400
Oh, but that...

00:19:18.780 --> 00:19:21.570
That's headed right for the old guy's post.

00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:33.110
Switch to fire arrows and concentrate
on the siege tower!

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:37.070
Fire!

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:42.110
What?! The flames--

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:43.860
Did they soak that thing in water?!

00:19:43.860 --> 00:19:45.110
Sir!

00:19:45.110 --> 00:19:47.690
Well, it <i>is</i> huge, all right.

00:19:47.690 --> 00:19:51.780
To see that massive thing move--
I can hardly believe my own eyes.

00:19:51.780 --> 00:19:55.530
It would seem Gi is home
to some excellent designers.

00:19:57.030 --> 00:20:00.440
And? So what?

00:20:00.440 --> 00:20:02.610
A Gi siege tower, eh?

00:20:02.610 --> 00:20:04.820
It's of considerable size, but still...

00:20:04.820 --> 00:20:09.690
Siege towers have been
well-studied for many long years.

00:20:09.690 --> 00:20:18.070
Kankoku Pass was built with the tallest possible
still-mobile siege tower in mind.

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:20.780
No matter how massive the siege tower,

00:20:20.780 --> 00:20:23.360
it still won't reach the top of Kankoku Pass.

00:20:26.440 --> 00:20:28.030
No!

00:20:29.280 --> 00:20:31.030
But of course!

00:20:33.110 --> 00:20:37.230
Hey! You need more height! It's not gonna reach!

00:20:41.230 --> 00:20:42.320
Why, you...

00:20:43.400 --> 00:20:45.570
You clutch of imbeciles!

00:20:45.570 --> 00:20:49.860
Did you think that thing would clear Kankoku Pass?

00:20:49.860 --> 00:20:52.320
You don't know <i>anything</i> !

00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:56.110
You don't have the slightest clue
what Kankoku Pass really is!

00:20:56.110 --> 00:20:59.690
Built with buckets of blood and sweat
shed by the people of Chin,

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:06.610
with life itself going into constructing
its height, its sturdiness!

00:21:06.610 --> 00:21:10.940
And so, in the hundred-some years
since Kankoku Pass came into being,

00:21:10.940 --> 00:21:13.820
no enemy has ever once breached it!

00:21:13.820 --> 00:21:15.570
Not <i>once</i> !

00:21:15.570 --> 00:21:17.980
N-Not even once?

00:21:17.980 --> 00:21:21.820
And you think you can
do better than that history?

00:21:21.820 --> 00:21:26.860
You think your hands have any
hope of reaching these walls?

00:21:26.860 --> 00:21:29.690
No enemy of Chin will ever pass these gates--

00:21:29.690 --> 00:21:33.230
not now, and not in the hundred years to come!

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:35.110
And <i>that</i>

00:21:35.110 --> 00:21:39.070
is Chin's national gate: Kankoku Pass!

00:21:48.940 --> 00:21:51.320
Huh? They're still advancing!

00:21:53.150 --> 00:21:56.480
They <i>know</i> it won't reach.

00:21:56.480 --> 00:21:59.650
There must be some gimmick.

00:22:08.320 --> 00:22:09.820
Halt!

00:22:24.150 --> 00:22:27.320
What an eyesore. Cover it in fire arrows!

00:22:27.320 --> 00:22:29.190
It has to catch eventually.

00:22:37.900 --> 00:22:39.400
You fools.

00:22:46.780 --> 00:22:48.110
Weights?

00:23:02.480 --> 00:23:04.150
Oh...

00:23:04.150 --> 00:23:05.780
...it'll reach.

00:23:14.980 --> 00:23:19.570
I designed it to take on Kankoku Pass!

